# the idle sweep (TUI-DESIGN-3 §3.4, §3.9): settle, then 12 s alone — exactly one pass (16 written frames at 250 ms, k = 1..16) lands in
# [6 s, 11 s] after the settle; run-smoke.sh counts the frames between the caption frame and the marker key's echo (14–18), checks that
# every one is ≤ 3 KB, that its letters equal the settled frame's (colour only: the band cells carry the `sweep` SGR), zero clears, 11 rows
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect step 0/
expect ◆(?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*\d+\.\d+\.\d+
mark settled
expect sess \$
sleep 12
mark idled
send h
expect (?:›|>) (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*h
send \x03
expect Say hi
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
